title: Denial Intelligence › A denial opened › Recommended next step
route: /denials/D-3290
intro: FLO recommends ONE step, from a fixed list of six, worked out from the denial type, what the request itself shows and the route the analysis already prefers. It shows as the 'Recommended' pill on that route in Your options (and its button is the primary one while nothing is under way), as the next step of a row still to decide on the dashboard, and, with its reasons, in the 'Compare the options' panel. It is a recommendation for a person to review, never a payer rule.
dir: TD
also: The mapping lives in one function (lib/step.ts, recommendedStep). 'Ask for reconsideration' is on the list but no demo denial maps to it: the demo has no payer rule that names it, and none is invented.
---
start s1 "A denial with nothing under way is on screen\nChip 'Analyzed' or 'Resubmitting'"
agent a1 "FLO reads the denial type, the request (a resubmission path, time left on its window) and the analysis (win chance, which route it prefers)"
decision d1 "Is it a retro-authorization denial?"
decision d2 "Does the analysis say accept?\n(win chance under 35)"
decision d3 "Late notice or full denial, and does the request have a resubmission path?\n(type 'Resubmission' or a 'to resubmit' clock)"
decision d4 "Which route does the analysis prefer?"

screen w1 "Accept"
screen w2 "Investigate by hand"
screen w3 "Correct and resubmit"
screen w4 "File an appeal"
screen w5 "Peer-to-peer review"
process w6 "'Ask for reconsideration' is the sixth word on the list\nNo demo denial maps to it: that needs a payer rule that names it, and none is invented"

process n1 "A retro denial turns on dates and coverage status: accept when the analysis says so, otherwise a person checks the dates first"
process n2 "'File an appeal' when the clock running is the one to file or resubmit, the call window has closed, or the notice was late"
process n3 "'Peer-to-peer review' while the call window is open"

screen blk "Your options: 'Recommended' on that route, its button primary\n'Investigate by hand' picks no route: a pill with the word sits in the card header\nThe written choice is titled 'Correct and resubmit' for that word"
screen opt "Dashboard: the row's Next step reads the word ('Accept', 'Correct and resubmit')\nCompare the options: the same route is selected"

click b1 "Click 'Accept the decision'"
click b2 "Click 'Book a call'"
click b3 "Click 'Draft the appeal'"
click b4 "Click 'Draft the corrected request'"
process pf "No route is picked: the person reads the findings and the eligibility dates, then chooses any of the three"
goto g1 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Accept the denial"
goto g2 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Peer-to-peer › Book the call"
goto g3 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Written appeal › Confirm and draft"
overlay o4 "Confirm 'Confirm the next step: correct and resubmit'\n'Draft the corrected request' or 'Cancel'\nThe same letter flow follows: Advocate drafts, a clinician signs, Navigator files"
goto g4 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › A denial opened › Where the denial is weak"

click wy "Click 'Compare the options'"
screen wr "Under the radio cards: 'Why FLO suggests correct and resubmit'\nThe type and payer, and the read\nThe chances of a call and of a written appeal, from N similar decisions (or a benchmark estimate)\nThe window left, the rule that chose the route\n'This is a recommendation for a person to review. It is not a payer rule.'"
goto gc "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Your options"
end e1 "The person picks a route"

s1 --> a1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| d2
d2 -->|Yes| w1
d2 -->|No| w2
d1 -->|No| d3
d3 -->|Yes| w3
d3 -->|No| d4
d4 -->|Accept| w1
d4 -->|Written appeal| w4
d4 -->|Call| w5
d1 -.-> n1
d4 -.-> n2
d4 -.-> n3
a1 -.-> w6
w1 & w2 & w3 & w4 & w5 --> blk
blk --> opt
w1 --> b1 --> g1
w5 --> b2 --> g2
w4 --> b3 --> g3
w3 --> b4 --> o4 --> g3
w2 --> pf --> g4
blk --> wy --> wr --> gc
wr --> e1
